# Wildcards and quotes
> AmigaDOS patterns use `#?` for any text. In vsh the shell expands `*` (any text) and
> `?` (one character) before the command runs.
$ touch a.txt b.txt c.log
? List only the files that end in .txt.
= grep -q a.txt "$LEARN_OUT" && grep -q b.txt "$LEARN_OUT" && ! grep -q c.log "$LEARN_OUT"
~ ls *.txt
! ls *.txt
? List the files whose name is one character plus .log.
= [ "$(cat "$LEARN_OUT")" = c.log ]
~ ls ?.log
! ls ?.log
> A name with a space must be in quotes, or the shell sees two words.
? Make a file called my notes.txt (with the space).
= [ -f "my notes.txt" ]
~ touch "my notes.txt"
! touch "my notes.txt"
